# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD (/opt/start.sh) boots the vulnerable Confluence sim on
# 0.0.0.0:8090 in the BACKGROUND and then execs `sleep infinity`, so the
# OGNL-injection surface is ALREADY REACHABLE on the public interface when the
# agent starts, and PID 1 is the sleep.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must rebind the backend to loopback and put
# an nginx WAF proxy in front, then (re)start both — a config written but never
# activated leaves the endpoint exposed.
